# Research repo stays text-free: raw/large/copyrighted data and checkpoints are NOT committed.
# Commit manifests, configs, code, docs, reports only.
#
# THIS REPO IS PUBLIC. The training corpus is derived from private agent sessions containing
# private source code and client-adjacent work. Nothing trace-derived is ever committed.

# ---- Trace-derived and merged corpora: NEVER commit ----
# Anchored with a leading slash so these match ONLY at the repo root. An unanchored `data/`
# matches any directory of that name at any depth, which silently swallowed the package source
# at src/suvadu/data/ on 2026-08-16 — the file was written, staged with `git add -A`, and simply
# never appeared. Ignore rules that are too broad fail quietly; that is what makes them
# dangerous.
/data/
/corpus/
*.jsonl
*.parquet
*.arrow
!docs/**/*.jsonl        # narrow exception: illustrative, hand-checked doc fixtures only

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
.venv-*/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
build/
dist/

# Model weights / checkpoints
runs/**/checkpoint*
*.pt
*.safetensors
*.bin
*.ckpt
*.gguf

# Logs / scratch
*.log
.tmp/
scratch/

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/

# ---- Internal-only tracking: local, never pushed to a public repo ----
# (Murai Labs global rule: internal trackers and audit trails stay local.)
GAPS.md
STATUS.md
CHECKPOINT.md
notes/
